@startuml bounded-contexts
title Agentic Delivery domain and infrastructure boundaries
left to right direction
package "Domain contexts" {
  rectangle "Agentic Delivery Governance" as governance
  rectangle "Agentic Delivery Control Plane" as control
  rectangle "Agentic Primitives" as primitives
  rectangle "Developer Distribution" as distribution
}
rectangle "Architecture Authority\nCross-context authority, not a bounded context" as architecture
rectangle "Public .github adapter\nCommunity health, issue forms, PR template" as public
rectangle "Private .github-private adapter\nProfile and approved agent-publication boundary" as private
rectangle "GitHub native Issue Type definitions" as nativeTypes
rectangle "Organization issue-field definitions\nLifecycle Stage + Delivery State" as fieldDefinitions
rectangle "GitHub Projects fields\nSeparate planning projection" as projects
rectangle "GitHub App installation\nRepository access + subscribed events" as app
rectangle "Repository Issues and pull requests" as issues
rectangle "Per-issue field values API\nRepository-scoped values" as fieldValues
rectangle "Participant contract in Control Plane\nEnrollment + immutable pins" as enrollment
rectangle "Consumer repositories" as consumers

architecture ..> governance : principles, language, cross-context ADRs
architecture ..> control : pinned architecture release
architecture ..> primitives : references
architecture ..> distribution : contracts
app --> control : grants access and supplies events
enrollment --> control : independently checked
control --> nativeTypes : reads issue type identity
control --> fieldDefinitions : reads definitions and option IDs
control --> fieldValues : reads/writes validated per-issue values
control --> issues : origin-scoped work operations
governance ..> nativeTypes : issue classification semantics
governance ..> fieldDefinitions : lifecycle and delivery semantics
public --> issues : GitHub defaults; form/type binding unverified
primitives --> private : reviewed projection target
primitives --> distribution : primitive release
control --> distribution : pinned workflow-bundle source
distribution --> consumers : versioned bootstrap and projection

note bottom
  Native Issue Type definitions and organization issue-field definitions are
  separate organization settings; issue values use a repository-scoped API.
  Projects fields are separate. The App does not distribute templates. Shown
  links are target contracts unless the live evidence snapshot says otherwise.
end note
@enduml
